'Phase15 suite checks random residuals, selected zero/one/alternating/geometric/impulse inputs, exact counts, same-helper FFT equality, inverses and numerical Gram. Main checks direct DFT/sparse oracle through N=1024 and shared-helper FFT at N=2048; separate large_smoke reaches N=16384. These are intended checks, not runs in this audit. Small direct DFT is the stronger independent algorithmic oracle.',
'Standard library only: Counter (unused), dataclass and lru_cache. Three assigned consumers rely on this exact hash. Bare imports and execution environment remain unpinned.',
[{'severity':'medium','lines':'180–200','finding':'Externally supplied cycles can duplicate or omit output labels while still consuming exactly N input elements. The helper lacks a permutation/disjoint-cover guard; correctness requires canonical cycles from orbits(N,B).'}, {'severity':'medium','lines':'121–177, 180–206','finding':'The public structural parameter guard admits N beyond the available fixed-field root range, which is rejected only later in the full pipeline. Early root-domain validation would prevent wasted work.'},{'severity':'info','lines':'7–11, 95–114, 203–207','finding':'Butterfly conservation is an architecture accounting result, not a lower bound on all FFT implementations. It already rules out a speedup claim for this concrete butterfly decomposition.'}],
